 concrete prerequisite ticket id and record a depends_on edge, then reference the symbol as `cross_session_warning_for [rebar:<id>]` wherever the ACs/testing invoke it.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the Scope to enumerate the actual emit-site packages (src/rebar/_commands/{leaf,composer,link_revert,transition}.py and src/rebar/_engine_support/{reads,gates}.py) rather than only src/rebar/_cli/, since the resolved-id points where the WARN is written live in the handler modules, not the dispatch layer.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search for 'resolve_ticket_id' under src/rebar/_cli returns (no matches); _execute.py only routes (name, rest) and never resolves ticket ids","resolved-id points are in rebar._engine_support/reads.py:345,504 (show/deps), gates.py:81 (check-ac), leaf.py/composer.py (require_id calls), link_revert.py:269 (link/unlink), transition.py:565 (transition/reopen)","plan concedes 'require_id ... is only one of the id-resolution paths ... some reads such as show/deps and the gate commands resolve their id on their own arm'"],"finding":"The Scope bullet localizes the code edit to 'src/rebar/_cli/' (the dispatch layer), but the emit must happen at each allowlisted command's resolved-id point, and none of those points are in src/rebar/_cli/ — they live in src/rebar/_commands/** (leaf.py, composer.py, link_revert.py, transition.py) and src/rebar/_engine_support/** (reads.py, gates.py). Those touched modules are not enumerated in Scope.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcb8df4d02bd89524","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope, first bullet ('The CLI dispatch layer under src/rebar/_cli/ ... add the stderr emit at each allowlisted command's resolved-id point')","norm_id":"nb6a7a888039d986f","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer scoping the diff to src/rebar/_cli/ only would have nowhere to put the emit, since id resolution occurs in the handler packages after dispatch"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Split the Scope: keep the allowlist frozenset in src/rebar/_cli/, but list the handler modules under src/rebar/_commands/ and src/rebar/_engine_support/ as the modules receiving the per-command emit call at their resolved-id points.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the positive rationale for emitting per-command at each handler's resolved-id point rather than centrally at `_execute.execute` — namely that the id is resolved only inside each handler (argv positions vary; link/unlink have two endpoints), so a central chokepoint keyed on raw `rest` cannot reliably extract the primary ticket id.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.468,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["`src/rebar/_cli/_execute.py:29` `execute(name, rest)` is the single dispatch chokepoint but receives raw unparsed `rest` argv — the ticket id is resolved only inside each handler (`require_id` or the command's own arm)","Plan: 'the implementation confirms each allowlisted command's resolved-id point during implementation and emits there' vs 'evaluated at the dispatch layer — not a single shared id-resolution helper'","A centralized execute()-level emit would resolve rest[0], but argv positions vary (flags may precede the id; link/unlink have two endpoints), so per-command placement after each parse is the robust choice — this is the missing rationale"],"finding":"The plan chooses per-command emission at each of 14 handlers' resolved-id points but does not state the positive rationale for preferring this over centralizing the emit at the single dispatch chokepoint (`_execute.execute`, which already routes by command `name`). The natural reader question 'why not one central emit keyed by the frozenset at execute()?' is unanswered; the plan even calls the gate 'evaluated at the dispatch layer' while the actual dispatch layer (`execute`) holds only unparsed `rest` argv with no resolved ticket id, creating apparent tension.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8e5a40b2d39987c6","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section: 'The gate that decides whether to emit is the allowlist frozenset ... evaluated at the dispatch layer' and 'each allowlisted command's resolved-id point'","norm_id":"n226d4e7a1b196364","priority":0.132,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add one sentence to the Approach: 'The emit is placed per-command rather than at the single execute() chokepoint because execute() sees only unparsed argv; the primary ticket id is resolved inside each handler (positional order varies, and link/unlink carry two endpoints), so the frozenset names WHICH commands warn while each command emits at its own already-resolved id.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"0545e898327a97b3","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["546d7a7d17667062",6583],"description_boxes":["90a512a5b8a10706",0],"file_impact":["88763b3984